WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.800 --> 00:00:07.133
MORGAN FREEMAN: I was a little
kid during World War II.

00:00:07.133 --> 00:00:10.600
And following the end
of the war, of course,

00:00:10.600 --> 00:00:18.333
glory and bravery and
patriotism instilled in me.

00:00:18.333 --> 00:00:20.567
And where do I go?

00:00:20.567 --> 00:00:21.767
Air Force.

00:00:21.767 --> 00:00:23.166
How'd you feel going in?

00:00:23.166 --> 00:00:26.000
So when I joined
the military, I really

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:28.000
did it to serve my country.

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:29.400
But when I got to
the drone base,

00:00:29.400 --> 00:00:30.800
I didn't know what I was doing.

00:00:30.800 --> 00:00:33.200
They didn't tell me
anything until I got there.

00:00:33.200 --> 00:00:35.967
They put me in a small
theater with about 25

00:00:35.967 --> 00:00:37.433
other individuals.

00:00:37.433 --> 00:00:40.066
And then they played a montage
video of drone strikes.

00:00:40.066 --> 00:00:42.834
[explosions]

00:00:45.633 --> 00:00:48.734
And Sergeant, after it's done,
he's standing at parade rest.

00:00:48.734 --> 00:00:51.800
He's like, your job is to
kill people and break things.

00:00:51.800 --> 00:00:57.233
And I was just like, holy
[bleep],, what am I doing?

00:00:57.233 --> 00:00:59.133
MORGAN FREEMAN: What is
it like flying a drone?

00:00:59.133 --> 00:01:04.333
BRANDON BRYANT: I was an MQ-1
Bravo Predator sensor operator.

00:01:04.333 --> 00:01:06.667
So I controlled the
camera and the missiles.

00:01:06.667 --> 00:01:08.133
Like, that's my job.

00:01:08.133 --> 00:01:11.367
The pilot keeps the
aircraft in the air.

00:01:11.367 --> 00:01:14.700
And basically, we
support one another.

00:01:14.700 --> 00:01:16.500
If you look out the
window, actually,

00:01:16.500 --> 00:01:20.700
if you look down there, that's
kind of the same paradigm view

00:01:20.700 --> 00:01:22.000
that we had.

00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:25.066
If there's a target to be
attacked, they're like, OK,

00:01:25.066 --> 00:01:26.433
this is what's going on.

00:01:26.433 --> 00:01:27.900
Or you're going
to watch a person

00:01:27.900 --> 00:01:29.433
outside this guy's house.

00:01:29.433 --> 00:01:31.066
I mean, you're just waiting
for an opportunity for them

00:01:31.066 --> 00:01:33.166
to get into a location, and
you're going to shoot them.

00:01:33.166 --> 00:01:35.700
[explosion]

00:01:35.700 --> 00:01:38.133
MORGAN FREEMAN: Do you
know how many kills?

00:01:38.133 --> 00:01:40.333
13 directly.

00:01:40.333 --> 00:01:45.834
My first shot, it was winter,
mountains of Afghanistan.

00:01:45.834 --> 00:01:46.834
I killed three people.

00:01:46.834 --> 00:01:50.000
[explosion]

00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:51.567
Two of them were
obliterated into pieces.

00:01:51.567 --> 00:01:53.900
And one of them,
watched him bleed out

00:01:53.900 --> 00:01:56.233
and then watched an infrared
become the same color

00:01:56.233 --> 00:01:59.200
as the ground that he died on.

00:01:59.200 --> 00:02:01.333
MORGAN FREEMAN:
Is there remorse,

00:02:01.333 --> 00:02:04.400
or there was like consternation?

00:02:04.400 --> 00:02:05.900
BRANDON BRYANT: I'm
sitting there like, I

00:02:05.900 --> 00:02:07.700
just watched a man bleed out.

00:02:07.700 --> 00:02:08.967
I felt horrible.

00:02:08.967 --> 00:02:10.533
I wanted to cry.

00:02:10.533 --> 00:02:13.133
I felt-- you know, you feel,
the "this is what I just did,"

00:02:13.133 --> 00:02:14.233
the adrenaline rush.

00:02:14.233 --> 00:02:17.200
I mean, it was all
sorts of weird--

00:02:17.200 --> 00:02:18.667
weird feelings.

